  "bs_repo_id": {},
  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:94501",
  "description": "The fence-agents packages provide a collection of scripts for handling remote power management for cluster devices. They allow failed or unreachable nodes to be forcibly restarted and removed from the cluster.   \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * pyjwt: pyjwt: Authentication bypass via empty HMAC key acceptance (CVE-2026-102266)\n  * pyjwt: PyJWT: Authentication bypass via improper public key validation (CVE-2026-102268)\n  * pyjwt: PyJWT: Authentication bypass via acceptance of DER public keys as HMAC secrets (CVE-2026-102271)\n  * pyjwt: pyjwt: Verification key substitution via unvalidated JWKS redirects (CVE-2026-102267)\n  * pyjwt: pyjwt: Token forgery via improper Unicode byte-order mark handling (CVE-2026-102272)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
  "fromstr": "packager@almalinux.org",
  "issued_date": {
    "$date": 1793664000000
  },
